ctangular anchors of the same size sit on opposite\n  diagonal corners, with the first anchor above-left of the second.\n- The upper-left anchor has two one-cell-thick vertical control bars to its\n  right and two one-cell-thick horizontal control bars below it.\n\nRule:\n- Copy the anchor rectangle into the two missing corners of the implied\n  larger rectangle.\n- Repeat the right-side control bars horizontally between the left and right\n  anchors, using their spacing as the period, and draw the outer top and\n  bottom borders in the first right-control color.\n- Repeat the below-side control bars vertically between the top and bottom\n  anchors, using the same period, and draw the outer left and right borders\n  in the first below-control color.\n\nKey insight: The small control bars are the first two ticks of two periodic\nframe patterns; the diagonal anchor supplies the opposite corner and the\nmissing two anchor copies.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"two same-color solid rectangular anchors, with two right control bars and two below control bars beside the upper-left anchor\",\n  \"dst\": \"the missing two anchor corners and periodic frame segments between all four anchors\",\n  \"transform\": \"copy the anchor rectangle into the missing corners; repeat the right-control colors across the top and bottom anchor rows and outer borders, and repeat the below-control colors down the left and right side bars using the same spacing\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"b25e450b\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4043\nmechanism=0.4708\nlexical=0.0210\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:rectangle, operation:recolor, operation:sort_order, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/b25e450b.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/b25e450b.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide each black border rectangle to the opposite border, recoloring its swept stripe orange and leaving the rectangle black at the far edge.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid contains black rectangular 4-connected masks, each touching exactly one outer border.\n- Grey cells form incidental pattern content; orange is the trail color used when a black mask slides.\n\nRule\n- Treat all black rectangles as moving simultaneously.\n- A rectangle touching the top or bottom edge moves vertically to the opposite edge in the same columns.\n- A rectangle touching the left or right edge moves horizontally to the opposite edge in the same rows.\n- Recolor the complete swept row or column stripe to orange, then stamp every destination rectangle in black.\n\nKey insight\n- Edge contact gives the slide direction; the output is the set of opposite-edge black rectangles plus their orange trails.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"black rectangular mask s touching exactly one outer border\",\n  \"path\": \"straight slide from s to the opposite border along its row band or column band, determined by the touched border\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"recolor the complete swept row/column stripe orange, then place s at the opposite edge\",\n  \"transform\": \"all black masks move simultaneously; destination black masks overwrite orange trails and any grey cells, while cells outside swept stripes remain unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e4888269\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3578\nmechanism=0.4513\nlexical=0.0146\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, operation:recolor, operation:sort_order, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e4888269.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/e4888269.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRecolor every target pixel by following the ordered two-column substitution legend.\n\nInput structure\n- A dominant background surrounds one multicolor vertical legend: a connected,\n  fully filled two-column block with one color pair per row.\n- Other non-background pixels or objects are the targets; divider or frame\n  pixels are ordinary target-side structure that remain unchanged unless their\n  color is rewritten by the legend.\n\nRule\n- Read the legend rows from top to bottom as substitutions from the left\n  column color to the right column color.\n- For each non-background pixel outside the legend, scan those rows in order;\n  whenever the current color equals the row's left color, replace it with the\n  row's right color and keep scanning lower rows.\n- Leave the legend itself and background pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The same color may be rewritten multiple times, but only by substitutions\n  that appear later in the vertical legend, so the row order is part of the\n  symbol instruction.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use the two-column legend as ordered color substitutions and recolor every non-background target pixel outside the legend.\",\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"non-background pixels outside the unique fully filled two-column legend\",\n  \"transform\": \"replace each target pixel color with the final color reached by the ordered substitutions; keep the legend and background unchanged\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"the two-column legend maps each row's left color to that row's right color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"for each target pixel, scan legend rows top-to-bottom while carrying the current color, so later rows can rewrite earlier substitution results\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"ff2825db\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3323\nmechanism=0.4242\nlexical=0.0190\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbo