\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Several solid 5×5 monochrome blocks, each a distinct non-bg color.\n- For each block color, a small same-colored motif sprite elsewhere on the grid.\n\nRule:\n- Match each motif to its same-colored 5×5 block.\n- Center the motif within the block and recolor those cells to bg (punching holes).\n- Pack all carved blocks into an output grid preserving their original row/column order, separated by 1-cell gaps and a 1-cell outer border.\n\nKey insight: The motif acts as a stencil — it's not stamped onto the block but carved out of it as background holes.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"motif sprites s (small components)\",\n  \"dst\": \"center on solid 5x5 block sprites d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.color == d.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"s.color -> bg\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"packed grid of carved blocks (1px border + 1px gaps, row/col order preserved)\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"985ae207\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3064\nmechanism=0.3578\nlexical=0.0155\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:rectangle, operation:sort_order, output:same_size, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/985ae207.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/985ae207.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRepeat each 3x3 control-center sprite toward the matching solid rectangle until a copy first overlaps that rectangle.\n\nInput structure\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
